---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — WhatsInMyPDF"
  description="No upload, no storage, no tracking of file contents. WhatsInMyPDF processes every file locally in your browser."
  pathname="/privacy"
>
  <section class="container max-w-2xl py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-muted-foreground">
      No upload, no storage, no tracking of file contents. When you open a PDF with this tool, it
      is read and scanned entirely inside your browser. The file is never sent to a server, never
      written to disk by us, and never inspected by anyone but you.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      This site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits. It sets no cookies and does not
      follow you across sites; it records the page URL, the referring page, and page-load timings.
      It runs on the page like any other script, so it can see which page you are on — but the
      scan itself never leaves your browser, so the file you scanned, its name, and its findings
      are not part of what it, or anything else, reports.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      No other third-party script runs on this site. The page's Content Security Policy allows
      scripts from this domain and from Cloudflare's analytics domain, and nothing else — a
      browser will refuse to load anything beyond that list.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      If you have questions about this policy, open an issue on the project's GitHub repository.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
